{"title":"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a cyclic quadrilateral. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the feet of perpendiculars from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb0f1d8a43539dbc3355734bafb2bfd855b5f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CA}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f7ea843ca22572caaff306acba3190f9e293b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ=QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> if and only if the bisectors of angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840cb55c82434b9ae047760636a017e9441e6ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> meet on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/c/91c587b0c1e5de0bde79b9d8c36913c16dee04d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> is the Simson Line and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5ccd7cb06749c10665239c13804f6110f5365810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APDQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2ed99ebdd5bf7792ec61bb931524b70c65c58c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BPDR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9da4ad4267d4783c93cf2ea03414ebb96eabfb2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CQDR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is cyclic. By angle chasing we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/361e8fac57cd41519edbaf5a13d18fc7cdcaaa65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DPQ\\sim\\triangle DBC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b45f11fbd7298b011e5ec35092eb520b95bbbaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DQR\\sim\\triangle DAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />. Then by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83f7ea843ca22572caaff306acba3190f9e293b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ=QR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d40c7dda87a9400e1ed845efb4a947976520a9d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DC}{CB}=\\frac{DQ}{QP}=\\frac{DQ}{QR}=\\frac{DA}{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"209\" height=\"43\" />. Rearranging and using the angle bisector theorem we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO\" title=\"2003 IMO\">2003 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202448\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 135/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3582/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.615      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.615      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25814:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202448 and revision id 217426. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}